  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">223391_FY24_WFP_Myanmar - Demoso IDP Assistance Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the proposed programme is providing nutrition-sensitive, life-saving assistance to crisis-affected populations to enable them to meet their immediate food and nutrition needs. This will target long-term IDPs, newly displaced IDPs. Based on feasibility assessments and beneficiary preferences, cash transfer assistance will be used. This will therefore contribute to WFP strategic outcome 1: Crisis-affected people in Myanmar meet their food and nutrition needs all year round.
 
 This programme will incorporate focus on protection and conflict sensitivity and ensuring participation of women. Awareness creation on nutrition, gender-based violence, disability inclusion, food hygiene and financial literacy through Social and Behaviour Change Communication SBCC messaging.</narrative>
  </description>
